#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD0095-A expect=skipped domain=SUPPXX
#note "CORPUS-WIDE PIN of the absent-RDOMAIN skip: the rule declares Requirements.Variables.All [RDOMAIN], so a SUPP dataset without the column is reported SKIPPED before any binding is read. (Until wave 3, PLAN-per-row-functions, the referenced_domain_class OPERATION also answered LIBRARY_NOT_AVAILABLE on an absent column; the registry function would read the absent column as a constant, which is why the requirement - present on all four SD0095 rules - is the pin's reason now.)"
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset SUPPXX class=RELATIONSHIP label="Supplemental Qualifiers for XX"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col QNAM    type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QVAL    type=Char label="Data Value"
---
S1 | 001 | XXNOTE | Extra info
